# App version (`versionCode` / `versionName`)

## Goal

Bump **`ncarouselBaseVersionName`** (at least **patch**) and **`ncarouselLocalVersionCode`** (+1) when **publishing** app changes on **`main`**, so CI can create tag **`v<versionName>`** and a **new** GitHub Release. Add a matching Fastlane changelog (see `.cursor/rules/45-changelog-fdroid.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/50-commit-push-release-automation.mdc`).

Daily try-outs on **`dev`** / **`feature/*`** do **not** require these bumps (see `.cursor/rules/06-git-branch-workflow.mdc`).

## Gradle fields

- **`ncarouselLocalVersionCode`**: +1 on every **`main`** publish that ships app changes.
- **`ncarouselBaseVersionName`**: bump patch (or minor/major) so the public version string and git tag advance.
- **Same commit:** update `defaultConfig` literals `versionCode = <digits>` and `versionName = "<name>"` to match those vals (F-Droid checkupdates; see rule `62-fdroid-binaries-requirements-ncarousel.mdc`).

## CI note

On **GitHub Actions**, without `NCAROUSEL_PUBLISH_RELEASE_APK`, `versionCode` can use `1000 + GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER` and `versionName` `base+$run`. Published **`main`** release APKs use stable codes via `NCAROUSEL_PUBLISH_RELEASE_APK=true`. Keep local Gradle fields moving on each **store** publish so F-Droid metadata stays consistent.
